{"title":"Career Roadmap · Scientist Trainee (ISRO / DRDO / BARC)","role":"Scientist Trainee (ISRO / DRDO / BARC)","summary":"A Scientist Trainee in organizations such as Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO), Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO), and Bhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC) works in scientific research, experimentation, instrumentation, modelling, testing, and technology development.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Physics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Scientist Trainee in organizations such as Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO), Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO), and Bhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC) works in scientific research, experimentation, instrumentation, modelling, testing, and technology development."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Physics student, the strongest long-term route is generally:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Physics","M.Sc Physics / Applied Physics","Research/technical recruitment","Scientist/Research career"]},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc alone can provide a scientific foundation, but M.Sc/advanced specialization is usually important for serious scientist-track opportunities, especially for core R&D positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Physics, laboratory skills, programming, scientific computing, projects, internships"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"M.Sc Physics / Applied Physics, research projects, national-level examinations/recruitment preparation"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Scientist/Researcher, specialized R&D, advanced experimental or computational work"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Scientist, Principal Scientist, Technical Lead, Research Group Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Physics Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classical Mechanics"},{"text":"Mathematical Physics"},{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear Algebra"},{"text":"Differential Equations"},{"text":"Electricity & Magnetism"},{"text":"Waves and Oscillations"},{"text":"Experimental Physics"},{"text":"Scientific measurement"},{"text":"Error analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Core Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Build competence in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quantum Mechanics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Statistical Mechanics"},{"text":"Electromagnetism"},{"text":"Optics"},{"text":"Electronics"},{"text":"Solid State Physics"},{"text":"Nuclear Physics"},{"text":"Atomic Physics"},{"text":"Computational Physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Research Orientation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Quantum Mechanics"},{"text":"Nuclear/Particle Physics"},{"text":"Condensed Matter"},{"text":"Astrophysics/Space Physics"},{"text":"Plasma Physics"},{"text":"Materials Physics"},{"text":"Scientific Computing"},{"text":"Numerical Methods"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Technical writing"},{"text":"If the degree is a 4-year Honours/Research program, use the additional year for a substantial research dissertation/project."}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Skills to Develop"],"rows":[[{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Calculus, linear algebra, differential equations, complex analysis"}],[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Classical mechanics, Lagrangian/Hamiltonian mechanics"}],[{"text":"Electromagnetism"},{"text":"Maxwell equations, electromagnetic waves"}],[{"text":"Quantum"},{"text":"Schrödinger equation, operators, quantum systems"}],[{"text":"Thermal Physics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics, statistical mechanics"}],[{"text":"Optics"},{"text":"Int